# §222 — RED: the stale resume (AC-331…AC-333; D-129 F-24 A, D-130), on the downloader as 5a left it
# command: swift test --skip-build --filter ModelDownloaderStaleResumeTests   (this Mac: macOS 26.6.1, Xcode 27, Swift 6.4)
# MEASURED FIRST, and it corrected the premise: a partial removed CLEANLY from the daemon's folder before the
# resume is REFETCHED BY THE SYSTEM ITSELF — that row passes on today's code (a guard now, it says what the
# platform does). So run 13's POSIX 2 was a race inside the daemon, and 'a lost partial locks the download out'
# was an inference the code did not bear out. The real lock-out: resume data NOTHING can read (a .resume cut
# short by a kill mid-write) — the resumed task fails with no fresh data ('unsupported URL'), the stale file
# stays, and every later attempt fails the same way. RED: that row, and 'once, never a loop'. GREEN guards:
# the cleanly lost partial (the system's own refetch) and fresh resume data being kept (AC-333).

